<h1>Instructions &amp; Regulations</h1>

<div class="card">
  <h2>How your pay works — one trip, start to finish</h2>
  <p>A trip is <b>not</b> finished when you deliver. One complete trip is:</p>
  <p style="font-size:16px"><b>Order → Load out → Delivery → Empty return</b></p>
  <ul>
    <li>The <b>load-out ticket</b> sets the load's pay — overweight is judged from the cargo weight printed on it.</li>
    <li>The customer pays the company <b>only after the empty return is confirmed</b>. Until the empty-in ticket lands, that load's money is held — for the company and for you.</li>
    <li>Your weekly settlement is calculated <b>from your tickets</b>. A missing ticket means that part cannot be settled — upload every ticket the same day.</li>
    <li>Covering another driver's work (prepull) is paid <b>only with the terminal ticket</b> as proof. Detention is paid <b>only with the dispatcher's confirmation message</b>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><b>Send the tickets, and your pay takes care of itself.</b></p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Company rules (per contract)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Speed: No driving over 70 mph.</b> Violations get a warning; repeated violations can be grounds for termination of the contract.</li>
    <li>Never edit your driving records (ELD). Log editing is prohibited.</li>
    <li>Settlements are paid every Friday, one week in arrears (50% of gross − fuel − insurance).</li>
    <li>Fuel is settled at the TCS discounted price. Keep your receipts.</li>
    <li>Pick up and return your own containers (no pre-pull).</li>
    <li>Complete your vehicle inspection (DVIR) in the ELD app before driving, and report defects right away.</li>
    <li><b>No ticket — no settlement for that part.</b> A trip is complete only when the empty is returned and its ticket is uploaded.</li>
    <li><b>Never bobtail for personal use — no exceptions.</b> The company carries no bobtail (non-trucking) insurance. The tractor moves only with a trailer, on company business.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Driver Start Kit — what every driver brings</h2>
  <p>Bring everything on this list on your first day. It stays in your truck. If you are missing anything, tell the office <b>before</b> your first day.</p>
  <div class="groupbox">
    <h3>Documents</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>CDL</li>
      <li>DOT medical card</li>
      <li>TWIC card</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="groupbox">
    <h3>Tools — your own toolbox, riding in the side box</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Wrench &amp; socket set, screwdrivers, pliers, adjustable wrench, hammer</li>
      <li>Tire pressure gauge and tread depth gauge</li>
      <li>Flashlight or headlamp, with spare batteries</li>
      <li>Box cutter / utility knife — for seals and straps. It stays in the toolbox.</li>
      <li>Zip ties, electrical tape, spare fuses and bulbs</li>
      <li>Work gloves (2 pairs) and a hi-vis safety vest</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="groupbox">
    <h3>In the cab</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Phone mount and charging cable — your phone is mounted and hands-free on every trip. No exceptions.</li>
      <li>Bedding set (sheet, blanket, pillow) for long waits and rest breaks</li>
      <li>Cooler / water bottle and personal items for a full day out</li>
      <li>Sturdy work boots (steel toe preferred) and a rain jacket</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="groupbox">
    <h3>Not in the truck — leave at home</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Weapons of any kind. Ports, terminals, and customers prohibit them, and so does the company. Nothing loose in the overhead bins — work tools only, and they live in the toolbox.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Consequences</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>1st violation: Written warning.</li>
    <li>2nd violation: Settlement hold and meeting.</li>
    <li>Serious violations (drunk driving, ELD tampering, leaving without notice, etc.): Immediate termination.</li>
    <li>Drunk or drug-impaired driving is never tolerated. If caught, you will be terminated immediately and reported to the authorities.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Termination</h2>
  <p>If the contract is terminated, the company pays any unpaid settlement amounts on the regular settlement schedule. Company equipment (truck, iPad, etc.) must be returned immediately. See your signed Independent Contractor Agreement for details.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Ticket evidence</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Upload the ticket photo at each step: pickup = load-out EIR, delivery = POD, return = empty-in EIR.</li>
    <li>If you covered another driver's empty return or prepull, the prepull amount is credited <b>only if you uploaded that terminal ticket</b>.</li>
    <li>The full amount for a load can be collected only once the empty-in ticket is confirmed.</li>
    <li>Detention is 2 hours free, then $50 per hour — and it is paid <b>only for detention the dispatcher confirmed by message</b>. Enter the amount and the supporting message in the portal to claim it; once confirmed, it is added to your settlement.</li>
    <li>Upload the ticket for each step. Substitute return/prepull work is credited only with its terminal ticket. Detention pays only when the dispatcher confirms it by message.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

